    "updated_at": "2026-03-20T08:39:04Z",
    "body": "I've seen #12150, and I think it would solve my problem.\n\nThis proposal offers an alternative to addressing a narrower problem than #12150, which can be useful to pursue in case #12150 becomes stalled.\n\nThis proposal is still relevant even if #12150 is implemented. Why shouldn't I have the same ability to customize form submission imperatively that I do declaratively.\n\nAs an aside, I was genuinely surprised that based on the current APIs, the form seems to evaluate form overrides by reading the properties from the button directly. This suggests a race condition might occur if I were to modify a form override property on a button between when a submit is requested by that button and when the form actually submits.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
